course: dictionary
lesson: 11154
title: Willow: a tree and its wood
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A willow is a tree with long, thin, bendy branches and narrow leaves, and it often grows near water. The same word can also name the wood that comes from this tree. When you read about a cricket bat or a basket, the word means the wood.
explain: Read the words around an unknown word to find its meaning. «The Mole hears the wind playing in the reeds and rushes and osiers.» Reeds and rushes grow beside water, so the clues tell you that osiers grow there too. Osiers are willows with long, thin, bendy twigs.
explain: Some words sound the same but mean different things. «Pussy willow» is a kind of willow with soft, furry buds, not a cat. Check the words around the word before you decide what it means.
fact: A willow is a tree with long, thin, bendy branches and narrow leaves.
fact: Willows often grow near water, by rivers and ponds.
fact: A weeping willow has branches that hang down to the water.
fact: Willow wood is used to make cricket bats and baskets.
fact: Willow bark contains a natural substance that was once used to ease pain.
exercise: «The Mole hears the wind playing in the reeds and rushes and osiers.» What are osiers? | *Willows with long, thin, bendy twigs | Birds that sing at dawn | Tall grass on a hill | Small boats on the river
exercise: Sam says, «This cricket bat is made of willow.» What does willow mean here? | A tree that grows high on hills | A small bird that lives in reeds | A bat that flies at night | *The wood of the willow tree
exercise: Where do willows usually grow? | On the top of the highest mountain | In the desert, with no water at all | Deep inside a cave | *Near water, by a river or pond
test: When was «The Wind in the Willows» first published? | *1908 | 1980 | 1808 | 1995
test: Scientists say «wolves changed the rivers» is too simple. Why? | Because willows cannot grow near water | Because scientists never argue about anything | Because wolves never lived in Yellowstone | *Because bears, people and weather also mattered
exam: Which statement about willows is true? | Willow wood is only used to make paper | All willows have branches that hang down and cannot grow near water | Willows never grow near rivers or ponds | *Willows often grow near water, and their wood is used to make cricket bats
